{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>For the soul of all flesh — its blood is in its soul.</b> For the soul of a living creature is its blood — that is, the vaporous blood-spirit (Leviticus 17:7)." "<b>In its soul.</b> Together with the vital force borne within it. This is because the vaporous and subtle component of the blood is indeed the bearer of the vital force, and since it is the subtlest of the perishable bodily components, it is without doubt nourishment for demons and for those who seek their company." "<b>And I said to the children of Israel.</b> And apart from this, even though I permitted it to the children of Noah, I forbade it to Israel earlier in the section of צו (Leviticus 7:26), because the life of the living creature was within it during its lifetime, and one who is nourished from it is drawn back toward his bestial nature."], :book :leviticus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {0 "Sforno's verse citation reads ויקרא י\"ז:ז, but the cross-reference Leviticus 17:7 does not match this lemma, which is at 17:14; the citation may be corrupt or may refer to a related verse."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:36:44.711761507Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}